I have given up on there being any real chance of controlling outbursts of
extreme rudeness on this List. We've tried a system of "justice" in which
formal charges are filed, with the result that no justice prevails. We've
tried mechanistic systems of "proofs demanded" and "Polite Societies." Even
ideas of "shooting" one's opponents, figuratively.

(Few of these ideas have been actually given a good, solid test...and the
response says they're not likely to. The one major test of the "Polite
Society" was, in my opinion, a dismal failure.)

My solution? "If a post offends thee, pluck it out." That is, use the
delete command _liberally_ and _quickly_, and delete forever posts which
are rude, baiting, flaming, foolish, etc.

I simply don't respond to people who have been grossly rude to me, either
by baiting me or by questioning my competence in a schoolyard insult sort
of way.

Not that they're in my "kill file," as neither of my two mailreaders (elm
and Eudora) easily allow this. And I like to at least *see* what these
folks are posting, however briefly, before deleting their insults and
baits.

(Deleting their baits and insults is a great strategy, because it allows me
to mostly forget the posts ever happened and helps me to avoid responding
in kind. A couple of times I've been tempted to counter-flame someone, only
to realize with palpable relief that I had already deleted their posting
and hence was saved!)

Yes, I slip up at times, and I expect I will in the future. I'm hoping to
be even more consistent in this regard, as the alternative--for my peace of
mind--is to quit the List. 

(The new List software, with real Kill capabilities, by author and by
thread name, will be a good step toward making the List a survivable
experience. The "reputation markets" ideas, as with the upcoming HeX
system, is much less useful to me, as I don't really care what other people
think for the purposes of deciding what to read and what to delete...that's
just a popularity contest. Of use perhaps with a large (several hundred)
population of active posters, but of little use when we all know the couple
of dozen active posters.)

Meanwhile, if your postings are not being responded to by me, or by others
(who I hope will join me in this type of "Personal Polite Society"), you
might want to ask yourself if you've been obnoxious, sniping, and rude
lately.

Fellow Extropians, take control of your own peace of mind and help stamp
out obnoxious and baiting posters--become a secret member of the PPS and
simply ignore these buzzing irritants. Switch channels when they come on.
Ignore them. Boycott them, whoever they are (for you). It may teach them
some manners.

Cheers!

-Tim
